WEBVTT

01:51.381 --> 01:53.051
I'm so cold.

01:53.461 --> 01:54.631
Got any booze?

02:06.271 --> 02:07.941
A Gamble

02:08.021 --> 02:11.061
It's already autumn.

02:11.861 --> 02:14.781
Everything tastes good in autumn.

02:15.071 --> 02:19.491
Especially fish. Cod, trout, and herring!

02:20.071 --> 02:23.741
The pigs and sheep fatten up too, captain.

02:23.831 --> 02:25.871
That's right. It's great.

02:25.951 --> 02:30.461
I want some salted sausage
with some dark beer!

02:30.541 --> 02:32.291
Give me some.

02:32.381 --> 02:34.041
At first, I thought it was weird.

02:34.131 --> 02:36.881
But I got used to English beer.

02:36.961 --> 02:39.631
I like cheese with my beer.

02:39.881 --> 02:42.141
Cheddar had great cheese.

02:42.801 --> 02:44.761
Enough about food.
It's all about the women!

02:45.101 --> 02:48.391
The women here are so classy.
They're exactly my type!

02:48.481 --> 02:50.271
I know what you mean! They've got modesty.

02:50.351 --> 02:51.561
YOU MUST NOT COMMIT ADULTERY

02:51.651 --> 02:53.401
Maybe it's because they're Christian.

02:53.691 --> 02:56.191
Christianity is nice.

02:56.281 --> 02:59.151
It's popular these days. Maybe I should convert.

02:59.241 --> 03:00.911
I don't want to convert.

03:01.451 --> 03:04.831
If you're Christian, they're always telling
you not to do this or that.

03:05.331 --> 03:09.161
I saw a statue of the guy they worship
in London.

03:09.461 --> 03:11.921
He looked so weak.

03:12.001 --> 03:15.041
-You'll get punished for saying that!
-Yeah!

03:15.711 --> 03:17.671
He's so skinny.

03:17.761 --> 03:20.931
Thor could knock him out with his hammer
in an instant!

03:21.301 --> 03:24.181
I heard he's a magician.

03:24.261 --> 03:27.061
He does things like walking on water
and making more bread appear.

03:27.471 --> 03:29.311
That's some lame magic.

03:29.391 --> 03:32.941
Odin and Thor are better.

03:33.021 --> 03:34.651
Well, well.

03:34.731 --> 03:38.111
There's no need to jump to conclusions.

03:38.401 --> 03:42.571
Let's ask a Christian directly.

03:43.071 --> 03:44.451
Hey!

03:44.871 --> 03:46.331
Prince!

03:47.331 --> 03:50.411
Who do you think is better?

03:50.501 --> 03:52.831
Jesus, or the gods in Asgard?

03:56.041 --> 03:57.211
Well?

03:57.711 --> 03:59.591
I wonder what's wrong?

04:00.421 --> 04:04.091
Are you too shy to talk in front of everyone?

04:06.761 --> 04:08.851
Don't get so full of yourself, Thorkell!

04:09.311 --> 04:10.851
You infidel!

04:11.181 --> 04:14.141
Do you understand what you're doing?

04:14.231 --> 04:18.481
How dare you talk to
His Highness Canute with such impudence?

04:20.731 --> 04:22.531
Well,

04:22.611 --> 04:25.111
I don't like taking hostages either.

04:25.201 --> 04:26.321
But...

04:26.411 --> 04:28.951
King Sweyn is ignoring me.

04:29.581 --> 04:34.581
So, I thought maybe he'd notice me
if I captured the prince.

04:35.501 --> 04:39.091
I wish you'd try and understand how hurt I feel.

04:39.381 --> 04:42.461
Captain! You sound like a maiden in love.

04:42.551 --> 04:43.421
Yes!

04:43.511 --> 04:45.011
That's exactly it!

04:45.091 --> 04:48.431
I've fallen for King Sweyn.

04:48.511 --> 04:50.221
You're huge for a girl.

04:50.311 --> 04:52.471
You're the king of the Northern Sea,
after all!

04:52.561 --> 04:54.981
You really fell for him.

04:57.481 --> 04:59.651
You guys are all crazy.

04:59.731 --> 05:01.901
You know nothing but war.

05:02.651 --> 05:04.531
You're all going to die.

05:04.611 --> 05:05.861
How can 500 men

05:05.951 --> 05:09.701
defeat the Army of Denmark
and its 16,000 soldiers?

05:10.411 --> 05:12.081
We're not going to die.

05:12.161 --> 05:14.041
And we won't have a problem winning, Ragnar.

05:15.291 --> 05:18.251
You've been under the influence of Christianity
for a long time.

05:18.331 --> 05:20.501
Have you forgotten about...

05:21.501 --> 05:23.671
the honor of

05:23.761 --> 05:25.721
a Norman warrior?

05:28.141 --> 05:29.391
You mean Valhalla?

05:30.391 --> 05:31.641
That's right.

05:32.971 --> 05:34.641
The Valkyries

05:34.731 --> 05:37.771
are always on the lookout
for the souls of heroes.

05:37.981 --> 05:42.901
Heroes who deserve to be called
Einherjar, the warriors of the gods.

05:43.861 --> 05:45.781
Only those who have fought

05:45.861 --> 05:47.951
and died

05:48.031 --> 05:51.031
are allowed to live in the hall of warriors
in heaven.

05:55.161 --> 05:56.711
It's how you fight,

05:56.791 --> 05:58.961
and how you die.

05:59.041 --> 06:00.501
That's what matters.

06:01.501 --> 06:03.921
The stronger the enemy, the better.

06:06.971 --> 06:08.341
You're so old-fashioned.

06:08.721 --> 06:09.591
Is that so?

06:09.681 --> 06:13.221
It's because you're always running around
from battlefield to battlefield.

06:14.261 --> 06:15.971
You poor thing.

06:16.391 --> 06:18.731
You're just a child, Thorkell.

06:18.811 --> 06:20.191
You don't know anything

06:20.941 --> 06:22.441
about the royal court,

06:22.521 --> 06:24.781
about King Sweyn,

06:24.861 --> 06:27.861
or about my prince, Canute.

06:29.611 --> 06:31.241
So?

06:31.321 --> 06:32.281
What do you mean?

06:36.371 --> 06:37.501
I can see him!

06:38.291 --> 06:41.001
Lord! It's you!

06:41.081 --> 06:43.041
-He's out of booze!
-I'm your disciple!

06:43.541 --> 06:45.381
-I'm right here!
-Priest! Priest!

06:45.461 --> 06:46.421
Please sit down!

06:47.091 --> 06:48.261
Get him some booze!

06:48.341 --> 06:49.761
-Open my eyes!
-Hurry!

06:49.841 --> 06:51.591
Get him something strong!

06:51.681 --> 06:54.431
Show me your love!

07:00.021 --> 07:01.851
It's always so funny!

07:02.521 --> 07:05.481
Incredible! It must be hard being Christian!

07:06.861 --> 07:07.901
Hey!

07:07.991 --> 07:09.111
Priest!

07:09.571 --> 07:11.201
What do you think?

07:11.281 --> 07:13.031
Jesus, or our god?

07:13.121 --> 07:14.491
Which one's better?

07:18.661 --> 07:20.871
Whichever one made booze.

07:24.711 --> 07:26.671
You're right!

07:26.751 --> 07:28.671
The booze will save us!

07:28.761 --> 07:31.051
Nice one, Christian!

07:46.771 --> 07:47.771
What's wrong?

07:47.861 --> 07:49.821
Why did you all stop?

07:50.191 --> 07:51.241
Captain.

07:56.451 --> 07:57.621
Right.

07:59.081 --> 08:01.331
Right about there!

08:08.801 --> 08:10.761
There they are!

08:10.841 --> 08:12.671
It's an ambush! The hill on the right!

08:15.051 --> 08:16.261
Damn!

08:16.351 --> 08:17.641
Thorkell!

08:17.721 --> 08:19.471
We've got you surrounded!

08:20.471 --> 08:24.231
We're Ragnar's troops, under Prince Canute!
We're 2000 strong!

08:25.601 --> 08:26.981
It's my men!

08:27.691 --> 08:28.981
Two thousand strong?

08:29.271 --> 08:32.031
It's usually a bluff when they announce it themselves.

08:32.111 --> 08:32.991
Hey.

08:33.071 --> 08:35.241
Yeah, I know.

08:35.701 --> 08:39.911
This is your last chance, you rebels.

08:39.991 --> 08:43.121
Release His Highness and Ragnar at once!

08:43.211 --> 08:45.621
If you do, we shall spare you this time.

08:46.671 --> 08:49.631
Think carefully about where you stand!

08:50.091 --> 08:51.171
You scoundrels...

08:51.261 --> 08:53.341
You have no...

08:53.421 --> 08:54.631
No...

08:54.721 --> 08:55.631
choice...

08:57.431 --> 08:58.851
Your Highness!

08:58.931 --> 09:00.391
Ragnar!

09:00.471 --> 09:02.771
Good. Very good.

09:02.851 --> 09:05.021
You're more honest than I thought.

09:06.351 --> 09:08.771
Followers of Ragnar!

09:08.861 --> 09:10.521
Thanks for your hard work.

09:10.981 --> 09:12.441
I will return His Highness

09:12.531 --> 09:15.401
Canute to you!

09:15.491 --> 09:18.411
There's no need to hesitate.

09:18.911 --> 09:20.031
Now then...

09:20.121 --> 09:22.541
show us your best attack!

09:22.621 --> 09:23.791
What?

09:25.331 --> 09:26.871
You bastard!

09:29.211 --> 09:30.041
Stop.

09:30.421 --> 09:31.551
Control yourself.

09:31.631 --> 09:33.171
We retreat!

09:33.261 --> 09:37.181
But there's no need to retreat as a warrior!

09:37.841 --> 09:39.431
They're not running away,

09:39.511 --> 09:41.601
and they don't fear imprisonment.

09:41.681 --> 09:42.931
If we retreat now...

09:43.021 --> 09:44.561
If we retreat now,

09:44.641 --> 09:46.941
we'd be called cowards.

09:47.391 --> 09:49.021
There is a reason for retreat.

09:49.101 --> 09:52.651
We must prioritize His Highness' safety!

09:52.731 --> 09:56.071
Victory means saving His Highness!

09:58.161 --> 10:01.201
Hey! What's wrong, guys?

10:01.281 --> 10:05.001
Are you scared? Even with 2000?

10:05.751 --> 10:07.211
Or is it something else?

10:07.791 --> 10:12.131
"We had to hold back because they had a hostage."

10:12.211 --> 10:13.551
Would it be easier

10:13.631 --> 10:16.211
to use an excuse like that?

10:16.301 --> 10:18.051
You bastard!

10:18.131 --> 10:19.381
How dare you?

10:19.471 --> 10:21.051
Stop!

10:21.141 --> 10:22.601
Didn't you hear my order?

10:23.061 --> 10:26.481
Don't let those war-hungry idiots provoke you!

10:28.441 --> 10:29.941
Sorry, sorry.

10:30.021 --> 10:30.981
Was what I said...

10:31.941 --> 10:34.151
the truth?

10:34.571 --> 10:36.651
How dare you?

10:36.741 --> 10:39.741
I'm sending you all to Valhalla!

10:41.031 --> 10:42.411
If you can,

10:42.491 --> 10:44.241
be my guest!

10:52.541 --> 10:53.461
Movement.

10:53.541 --> 10:55.461
They've started.

10:56.881 --> 10:58.921
Anyone could hear that.

11:00.511 --> 11:01.801
The wind's good.

11:02.391 --> 11:04.221
All right! Men!

11:04.301 --> 11:06.471
Let's do this just like we planned!

11:06.561 --> 11:07.601
Yeah!

11:24.701 --> 11:28.161
You idiots! Protect His Highness!

11:30.041 --> 11:32.671
This is turning out
the same way London did!

11:32.751 --> 11:34.581
Retreat!

11:34.671 --> 11:36.421
There's still time!

11:41.341 --> 11:43.091
Two thousand?
What are they talking about?

11:43.591 --> 11:45.471
They only have 400 max.

11:46.101 --> 11:49.021
This will be over in half an hour.

11:54.061 --> 11:55.311
What's wrong, captain?

11:56.731 --> 11:58.651
Don't you smell something?

11:58.731 --> 12:00.691
Something other than blood.

12:02.861 --> 12:04.571
You're right.

12:04.661 --> 12:05.871
I can't smell anything.

12:05.951 --> 12:07.871
It's the smell of intestines?

12:07.951 --> 12:08.871
No.

12:08.951 --> 12:10.501
It's upwind.

12:10.581 --> 12:12.371
The smell of charcoal.

12:19.341 --> 12:20.761
Charcoal?

12:31.021 --> 12:33.021
Hey! Get me some oil!

12:33.101 --> 12:34.941
Don't be so slow!

12:35.021 --> 12:36.021
Hurry!

12:36.101 --> 12:37.691
All right! That's good!

12:37.771 --> 12:38.941
Light it!

12:55.831 --> 12:57.541
This is bad.

12:57.631 --> 13:00.341
Captain! Where are you?

13:01.711 --> 13:02.711
Right here.

13:03.801 --> 13:04.841
We're in trouble.

13:04.931 --> 13:07.181
We're in the middle of an inferno!

13:07.261 --> 13:09.471
With all this smoke, we can't tell who's who.

13:09.761 --> 13:11.851
We can't fight like this.

13:12.221 --> 13:13.811
It's better downwind.

13:13.891 --> 13:14.731
Let's go.

13:15.271 --> 13:18.231
Dying in a forest fire won't get you to Valhalla.

13:18.311 --> 13:20.191
This isn't a forest fire.

13:21.191 --> 13:22.531
Someone set it on fire.

13:26.701 --> 13:29.201
It wasn't them.

13:30.201 --> 13:34.161
They wouldn't burn themselves
when they're here trying to save the prince.

13:35.291 --> 13:36.461
That means...

13:40.921 --> 13:43.211
A third party...

13:43.301 --> 13:44.511
is involved.

13:47.301 --> 13:48.761
It's burning.

13:49.091 --> 13:51.601
It hasn't rained in a few days.

13:54.681 --> 13:56.021
Horrible.

13:56.101 --> 13:57.891
There's a lot of ways to die.

13:57.981 --> 13:59.651
But I wouldn't want to die like that.

13:59.731 --> 14:01.111
Exactly.

14:01.191 --> 14:03.531
It's a painful and boring way to die.

14:04.191 --> 14:08.361
It'd help us out a lot if Thorkell died in this fire.

14:08.451 --> 14:11.281
That monster would never die from a tiny fire like this.

14:11.371 --> 14:13.581
I just want to confuse them for a while.

14:13.661 --> 14:14.541
Thorfinn!

14:15.621 --> 14:16.451
All right!

14:16.541 --> 14:17.541
Pour some water on him!

14:24.881 --> 14:27.381
You saw the prince from far away, right?

14:27.471 --> 14:29.551
He has a helmet with a feather and red cape.

14:29.631 --> 14:30.591
Don't get it wrong.

14:32.391 --> 14:34.011
All right. Go!

14:42.231 --> 14:43.651
Hey, Askeladd.

14:45.901 --> 14:49.821
Maybe we should have joined Ragnar's 400 men.

14:50.531 --> 14:53.831
Combined with our 100, we'd be even against Thorkell.

14:54.331 --> 14:55.991
We can't win being even.

14:56.911 --> 14:58.541
Even if we won,

14:58.751 --> 15:01.501
Ragnar's men would take the prize.

15:01.831 --> 15:03.841
-It's a deer!
-It's all or nothing.

15:03.921 --> 15:04.791
Get it!

15:04.881 --> 15:08.801
-Even if we end up burning Canute,
-It's venison!

15:08.881 --> 15:10.801
we'll just pretend we don't know anything.

15:10.881 --> 15:13.891
No one would ever find out we did it.

15:15.351 --> 15:16.601
That's what you say.

15:17.311 --> 15:20.191
You just think that Thorfinn can capture
the prince, right?

15:21.311 --> 15:23.151
Regardless of what you say,

15:23.231 --> 15:25.271
you actually trust him.

15:25.361 --> 15:26.611
That boy.

15:29.151 --> 15:31.241
It's just easy to make use of

15:31.321 --> 15:33.281
an idiot who's not afraid of anything.

15:40.661 --> 15:42.171
What's going on?

15:42.251 --> 15:45.421
Thorkell's not the one who did this.

15:45.501 --> 15:48.171
In any case, we must escape!

15:48.251 --> 15:50.051
Your Highness! Hurry!

15:56.351 --> 15:57.561
Ragnar!

15:57.641 --> 15:59.021
Idiot!

15:59.101 --> 16:02.941
What kind of man swings his sword without
seeing who he's attacking?

16:03.021 --> 16:04.151
Sorry.

16:04.481 --> 16:06.401
I was scared.

16:06.481 --> 16:09.821
What if you injured His Highness?

16:09.901 --> 16:11.401
You fool!

16:11.491 --> 16:12.951
Your Highness!

16:13.031 --> 16:14.411
Ragnar!

16:14.491 --> 16:16.491
Where are you?

16:16.871 --> 16:18.121
See?

16:18.201 --> 16:21.871
Smart men check first, just like that.

16:21.961 --> 16:23.581
I apologize, sir.

16:24.251 --> 16:25.381
Hey!

16:25.461 --> 16:27.251
His Highness is over here!

16:27.591 --> 16:28.591
Hey!

16:28.671 --> 16:30.301
We're on the same side!

16:30.381 --> 16:31.921
Please, just--

16:36.261 --> 16:39.351
We found Canute!

16:39.431 --> 16:42.431
-The prize! The prize!
-The prince is here!

16:42.521 --> 16:43.851
Over here!

16:45.151 --> 16:46.061
Damn!

16:46.151 --> 16:47.691
Damn! You're Thorkell's men!

16:48.651 --> 16:50.691
I'm the one who's the fool!

16:50.781 --> 16:52.691
Don't kill the prince!

16:53.031 --> 16:54.321
I know!

16:54.401 --> 16:56.111
We have to be careful, right?

16:56.611 --> 16:58.991
Over here, little boy.

16:59.081 --> 17:01.161
We're nice guys.

17:08.591 --> 17:10.211
That was close!

17:10.301 --> 17:11.211
A horse?

17:13.881 --> 17:15.431
Who's this kid?

17:18.261 --> 17:20.351
Why's he staring at us?

17:20.431 --> 17:22.721
He looks like he wants to fight.

17:22.811 --> 17:24.561
Are we allowed to kill him?

17:24.641 --> 17:27.101
Sure. He doesn't look like he's important.

17:27.191 --> 17:29.481
All right. It's decided.

17:29.811 --> 17:32.191
Die, kid!

17:39.071 --> 17:39.991
He disappeared?

17:52.301 --> 17:53.551
You there.

17:53.631 --> 17:54.921
You're Prince Canute, right?

17:56.221 --> 17:57.261
I've come to save you.

17:59.721 --> 18:01.181
Wait right there.

18:04.811 --> 18:06.141
Impossible.

18:06.231 --> 18:09.151
No one would come here to save the prince!

18:09.231 --> 18:10.311
But...

18:12.521 --> 18:13.941
Why?

18:14.031 --> 18:15.901
Why does His Highness

18:15.991 --> 18:18.531
never get to choose?

18:27.121 --> 18:28.291
Thorfinn!

18:28.371 --> 18:29.331
Hey!

18:29.421 --> 18:31.081
You're Thorfinn, right?

18:34.711 --> 18:36.011
Well, well!

18:36.091 --> 18:38.091
It's really you, Thorfinn!

18:38.421 --> 18:41.091
I knew I'd see you again!

18:41.511 --> 18:43.101
Thorkell!

18:43.181 --> 18:44.601
Captain!

18:44.681 --> 18:47.771
You guys were fighting him?

18:47.851 --> 18:49.351
He gave you a hard time, right?

18:49.731 --> 18:51.901
Thorfinn's a great warrior.

18:51.981 --> 18:55.111
He gave me this wound, after all.

18:55.781 --> 18:57.191
Look.

18:57.531 --> 19:00.361
If you underestimate him, you'll get hurt.

19:03.161 --> 19:04.581
Wait, Thorfinn.

19:04.951 --> 19:06.741
There's two things I want to ask you.

19:08.371 --> 19:11.501
You guys are behind this fire, right?

19:14.341 --> 19:15.251
One more.

19:16.131 --> 19:19.801
You called yourself Thors' son, right?

19:22.431 --> 19:24.471
Your father's name is Thors.

19:25.051 --> 19:26.811
And your mother's name is

19:27.431 --> 19:28.311
Helga.

19:30.561 --> 19:31.561
Am I wrong?

19:33.861 --> 19:35.271
How do you know that?

19:38.321 --> 19:39.991
I see, I see!

19:40.071 --> 19:44.161
So, you're the son of
the Troll of the Jomsvikings!

19:44.241 --> 19:46.581
That's why you're strong.

19:46.661 --> 19:48.951
The Troll of the Jomsvikings?

19:49.041 --> 19:50.661
He's Thors' son?

19:50.751 --> 19:52.421
He doesn't look like him.

19:53.331 --> 19:55.251
You know my father?

19:55.341 --> 19:57.421
Of course I know him!

20:00.051 --> 20:02.301
He's the only man in the world

20:02.381 --> 20:04.181
who's stronger than me.

20:05.681 --> 20:07.811
He's a true warrior.

20:14.481 --> 20:15.311
No!

20:22.951 --> 20:24.201
That's hot!

20:24.281 --> 20:25.531
Really hot!

20:25.621 --> 20:29.041
We don't have time to talk about the past,
Thorfinn.

20:30.081 --> 20:32.041
I'll give you the prince for now.

20:32.411 --> 20:33.751
Let's do this again.

20:35.631 --> 20:37.711
We're headed for the same place anyway.

20:38.001 --> 20:39.801
To King Sweyn's main forces!

20:39.881 --> 20:42.671
If you're able to escape me,

20:42.761 --> 20:44.631
you'll be victorious!

20:44.721 --> 20:47.351
Don't let me down,

20:47.431 --> 20:49.061
son of Thors!

20:49.351 --> 20:50.931
Thorfinn!

20:55.351 --> 20:56.561
Oh, dear.

20:56.901 --> 20:59.231
Where's Thorkell?

20:59.321 --> 21:01.191
Captain!

21:01.281 --> 21:02.571
Your Highness!

21:02.651 --> 21:04.151
Ragnar!

21:06.991 --> 21:09.031
You're with the enemy!

21:09.121 --> 21:10.031
You bastard!

21:10.121 --> 21:11.491
You're one of Thorkell's men.

21:18.961 --> 21:20.961
Thorfinn's late.

21:21.631 --> 21:23.461
You trusted in his luck

21:23.551 --> 21:25.471
too much this time.

21:26.591 --> 21:27.721
It doesn't matter.

21:27.801 --> 21:29.511
I didn't lose anything.

21:30.051 --> 21:31.141
There's more of them.

21:32.061 --> 21:33.601
Hurry up and take away your dead.

21:41.021 --> 21:42.321
Don't shoot!

21:42.401 --> 21:43.571
It's me!

21:43.651 --> 21:45.111
I've brought the prince!

21:50.321 --> 21:51.581
Yeah!

21:55.411 --> 21:57.501
Askeladd.

21:57.871 --> 22:00.331
Because of your reckless plan,

22:00.421 --> 22:02.461
my men got scattered.

22:03.251 --> 22:05.381
You'll pay for this dearly.

22:05.761 --> 22:09.431
You would have been destroyed
by Thorkell anyway.

22:09.511 --> 22:10.511
Be quiet.

22:11.011 --> 22:13.891
However, in this situation,

22:13.971 --> 22:17.851
I have no choice but to entrust the prince's safety
to you.

22:18.191 --> 22:20.021
Protect His Highness,

22:20.101 --> 22:22.611
and send the troops to the main army.

22:23.901 --> 22:25.651
I, Askeladd, son of Olaf,

22:26.191 --> 22:28.741
accept your request.

22:30.071 --> 22:31.491
Therefore,

22:32.581 --> 22:36.081
as his bodyguard, I would like to
look upon His Highness' face.

22:40.711 --> 22:41.541
Your Highness...

23:01.731 --> 23:03.021
Prince?

23:07.531 --> 23:09.861
Are you sure he's not the princess?
